// PathP type-equality / reflexivity — the DISCRIMINATING red->green for the
// TyPathP arm in Dispatcher.type_equal.
//
// Returning a value of type PathP(i, number, a, b) where the SAME type is the
// declared return type must be ACCEPTED (exit 0). Before the explicit TyPathP
// arm, type_equal had no PathP case and fell through to base_equal -> the
// FragCATT decidable `ty_structural_eq` (catt_r_yon.ml) ALSO has no PathP case,
// so it returns false for ANY two PathP — meaning even IDENTICAL PathP were
// FALSELY REJECTED (a false-reject on all path types, not the false-accept the
// old note claimed). classify_ty routes TyPathP to FragCATT, so the cubical
// fallback never runs for two PathP.
//
// With the arm (carrier up-to the bound interval-variable name + BOTH endpoints,
// modeled on the TyId arm + TyPi rename), identical PathP compare equal -> the
// program type-checks -> exit 0. The companion negative neg_pathp_endpoint.yon
// pins the other direction (different end endpoint -> rejected).
place Entry {
  fun reflPath(q: PathP(i, Number, a, b)): PathP(i, Number, a, b) { return q }
  fun main(): Number { return 0 }
}
